afe?",answer:"The short answer is yes. All communication is encrypted using SSL / HTTPS, our servers are backed up hourly, and zeroheight is hosted on enterprise grade cloud infrastructure via AWS S3. You can read more about their compliance and certifications here: <ul><li><a class='type_color-action underline hover-pointer' href='https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/'>AWS</a></li></ul>Access control is enforced using 22-character base64 authentication tokens. We never write our own security code and rely on industry best practices."},{question:"Are there any self-hosting options?",answer:"This isn't on the roadmap for now – we're currently focusing all our efforts on our cloud solution"},{question:"What’s the difference between a public share link and a private share link?",answer:"Private share links are one way to secure who can access your styleguide. Depending on your plan, you’ll have different options on how to secure your styleguides (<a href='https://zeroheight.com/3xlwst8/p/39cfd9-styleguide-security' target='_blank' class='type_color-action underline hover-pointer'>read more about this here</a>)."},{question:"Can I transfer ownership of a styleguide to a different account?",answer:"Yes! To transfer a styleguide to someone else, simply <span class='contact-link type_color-action underline hover-pointer'>get in touch</span> with us and we'll make it happen. If they don't have a zeroheight account, we'll help them set one up."},{question:"What are the payment options?",answer:" The Starter plan can be purchased by credit card from the billing page. The Enterprise plan can be purchased via invoice."},{question:"Can I switch or cancel anytime?",answer:"Yes. You can cancel your subscription anytime from the billing page (this will prevent it from renewing). You can continue using your cancelled account until the end of your billing cycle. Enterprise subscriptions have a 1 year minimum commitment."}],public:this.getOption("public"),teamPricing:n,companyPricing:o,c